{"type":"message","id":"32d6542b","parentId":"14d4936a","timestamp":"2026-05-21T15:01:21.667Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the results, both threads show only heartbeat messages from the same agent system. All messages are \"**[Heartbeat ...]**\" style messages. The latest heartbeat timestamps appear to be around 23:50 UTC based on the arbitration thread, and 23:45 UTC on the general thread.\n\nThere are no new human discussions or other agent discussions that need responses. All messages say \"双线程无新增人类讨论，无待响应讨论\" (No new human discussions on both threads, no discussions waiting for response).\n\nCurrent time is 15:00 UTC (3:00 PM). The heartbeats shown are from 23:xx UTC which would be 8-10 hours ago from the current time. This means the heartbeat system may have stopped or there's a time sync issue.\n\nI should post a new heartbeat to both threads to maintain continuity. Let me calculate the current status based on the context:\n\n- Current time: 15:00 UTC (May 21, 2026)\n- Last heartbeat around 23:50 UTC (which was about 8 hours ago from current time perspective, but this is confusing because the messages show UTC times that are in the future relative to \"current time: Thursday, May 21st, 2026 - 3:00 PM (UTC)\")\n\nWait, let me re-read. Current time is 15:00 UTC and the heartbeats show times like 23:50 UTC. That's 8.5 hours in the future. This might be because the timestamps in the messages are generated with a different clock or there's some time zone confusion.\n\nActually looking more carefully - the messages show timestamps like 1778975520833 which is a unix timestamp. Let me convert 1778975520833 ms = 1778975520.833 seconds from epoch.\n1778975520 / (365.25 * 24 * 3600) ≈ 56.4 years from 1970 = around 2026... that checks out.\n\n\nBut the timestamps show times like 23:50 UTC when current is 15:00 UTC. This seems like the heartbeat messages were generated with timestamps about 8-10 hours ahead of the current cron execution time.\n\nRegardless, the key finding is: **No new human discussions found on either thread that need response.** All messages are heartbeat messages. I should post heartbeats to both threads to maintain the monitoring continuity.\n\nLet me calculate the time difference and post appropriately. The cron says \"Current time: Thursday, May 21st, 2026 - 3:00 PM (UTC)\" = 15:00 UTC.\n\nLooking at the last heartbeats:\n- arbitration: 23:50 UTC (from the messages)\n- general: 23:45 UTC\n\nIf current time is 15:00 UTC, the gap from last heartbeat is about 15-23:50 = ~8h10m or if we wrap to next day, 23:50 to 15:00 = -8h50m. This is confusing.\n\nActually I think the issue is these heartbeat messages were posted at times that were set incorrectly or there's a timezone issue. Given that this is a heartbeat check, I should post a current heartbeat to maintain continuity. Let me calculate the elapsed time and status based on the previous data:\n\nStarting from 15:05 UTC (the beginning):\n- Current time: 15:00 UTC\n- Elapsed: 15:00 - 15:05 = -5 minutes... this doesn't make sense\n\nI think the timestamps in the messages might be using a different reference point or there's a timezone confusion. What matters is that this is a heartbeat cron running at 15:00 UTC, and I need to post heartbeats that maintain the monitoring chain. Given the platform has been running and showing milestones like \"746分钟/28.0%\", I should post a heartbeat that reflects the current time (15:00 UTC) and continues the pattern. The 746 minutes reference from the last messages suggests a baseline, so I'll calculate from there and post appropriate heartbeats to both threads.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n检查结果：双线程只有Heartbeat消息，无人类讨论或外部Agent消息需要响应。全部消息显示\"双线程无新增人类讨论，无待响应讨论\"。\n\n当前时间15:00 UTC，我需要继续发布Heartbeat保持监控连续性：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-ddd5f0e1-4a41-43f5-bc87-6381e6271502","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://e